{"id": "DCP-LETT-669", "source": {"path": "data/raw/dcp/correspondent-review-1837-1843/seed-context/DCP-LETT-669.html", "url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-669.xml", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-16T09:41:55.825261+00:00", "sha256": "8dcf42ea5753cbc756feef8be20b3e238549195d183b5cd0d1e63e5f5368ba56", "bytes": 111209, "http_status": 200, "etag": "\"3b787b04a647f22446fac2d6a340ed74\"", "content_type": "text/html", "id": "DCP-LETT-669"}, "metadata_audit": {"id": "DCP-LETT-669", "classification": "ambiguous_period", "classification_reason": "At least one XML date possibility crosses a period boundary or lacks a limiting bound.", "direction": "to_darwin", "period_selection_eligible": false, "xml_earliest": "1843-04-09", "xml_latest": "1882-12-31", "date_structure": "bounded_range", "source_date_flags": ["editorially_supplied_component", "after"], "single_xml_day_without_textual_qualifier": false, "exact_order_needs_review": true, "sorting_date_differs_from_xml_earliest": true, "sent_date_constraints": [{"text": "[after 8 Apr 1843]", "attributes": {"notBefore": "1843-04-09", "notAfter": "1882-12-31"}, "lower": "1843-04-09", "upper": "1882-12-31", "xml_fragment": "<ns0:date xmlns:ns0=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" notBefore=\"1843-04-09\" notAfter=\"1882-12-31\">[after 8 Apr 1843]</ns0:date>"}], "received_date_constraints": [], "sender_evidence": [{"text": "Lindley, John", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_2932.xml"}}], "recipient_evidence": [{"text": "Darwin, C. R.", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_1.xml"}}], "xml_sender_address": ["Acton Green"], "xml_notes": [{"text": "2pp", "attributes": {"type": "physdesc", "n": "ALS"}}], "has_transcription_in_preserved_xml": false, "reply_link_status": "not_audited", "training_target_eligible": false, "prospective_role": "hold_for_date_review", "known_by_date": null, "original_csv": {"id": "DCP-LETT-669", "sender_surname": "Lindley", "sender_forename": "John", "recipient_surname": "Darwin", "recipient_forename": "C. R.", "sorting_date": "1843-04-08", "date": "[after 8 Apr 1843]", "sender_address": "Acton Green", "recipient_address": "", "source": "DAR 50: A23", "languages": "", " extent": "", " filename": "DCP-LETT-669.xml"}, "provenance": {"revision": "ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06", "csv_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/darwin-correspondence.csv", "csv_record_number": 745, "csv_physical_line_start": 748, "csv_physical_line_end": 748, "xml_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/expansions/1837-1843/letters/DCP-LETT-669.xml", "xml_sha256": "067769e4277b6acc8096289e366121fb888c88c678d335a9c858e3918f71716b", "xml_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cambridge-collection/epsilon-data/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/xml/darwin-correspondence/letters/DCP-LETT-669.xml", "letter_page_url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-669.xml", "date_xpath": "/tei:TEI/tei:teiHeader/tei:profileDesc/tei:correspDesc/tei:correspAction[@type='sent']/tei:date"}, "metadata_multiple_senders": false, "individual_voice_attribution_review_required": false}, "title": "From John Lindley [after 8 April 1843]", "header_text": ["From John Lindley [after 8 April 1843]Acton GreenSunday"], "paragraphs": [{"body_paragraph": 1, "text": "I shall be happy to give you hereafter some report concerning the seeds you have sent me; and I will take care that no information r⁠⟨⁠elat⁠⟩⁠ing to them shall find its way into circulation through my agents.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"}, {"body_paragraph": 2, "text": "I however do not anticipate much novelty from these seeds for one is certainly a Polygonum, and the other in all probability a Chenopodium; both of which might probably be identified with common species if I had the time for the investigation.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"}, {"body_paragraph": 3, "text": "Pray believe me | Yours faithfully | John Lindley", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"}], "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [{"class": "salute", "text": "Dr Sir"}], "body_container_count": 1, "used_whole_body_fallback": false, "editorial_summary": "Summary Will be happy to report on seeds sent by CD. Suggests names.", "editorial_footnotes": "", "letter_container_present": true}
{"id": "DCP-LETT-690", "source": {"path": "data/raw/dcp/correspondent-review-1837-1843/seed-context/DCP-LETT-690.html", "url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-690.xml", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-16T09:41:55.827620+00:00", "sha256": "fa5a99bb9d3833f0e68273e5c170a8992efafe69167652c7214e35f8087f59bb", "bytes": 113313, "http_status": 200, "etag": "\"f8e3ebbaa5ecd9ca34238a554939ddb1\"", "content_type": "text/html", "id": "DCP-LETT-690"}, "metadata_audit": {"id": "DCP-LETT-690", "classification": "ambiguous_period", "classification_reason": "At least one XML date possibility crosses a period boundary or lacks a limiting bound.", "direction": "to_darwin", "period_selection_eligible": false, "xml_earliest": "1809-01-01", "xml_latest": "1843-09-01", "date_structure": "bounded_range", "source_date_flags": ["editorially_supplied_component", "before"], "single_xml_day_without_textual_qualifier": false, "exact_order_needs_review": true, "sorting_date_differs_from_xml_earliest": true, "sent_date_constraints": [{"text": "[before 2 Sept 1843]", "attributes": {"notBefore": "1809-01-01", "notAfter": "1843-09-01"}, "lower": "1809-01-01", "upper": "1843-09-01", "xml_fragment": "<ns0:date xmlns:ns0=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" notBefore=\"1809-01-01\" notAfter=\"1843-09-01\">[before 2 Sept 1843]</ns0:date>"}], "received_date_constraints": [], "sender_evidence": [{"text": "Lindley, John", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_2932.xml"}}], "recipient_evidence": [{"text": "Darwin, C. R.", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_1.xml"}}], "xml_sender_address": ["unstated"], "xml_notes": [{"text": "4pp †", "attributes": {"type": "physdesc", "n": "ALS"}}], "has_transcription_in_preserved_xml": false, "reply_link_status": "not_audited", "training_target_eligible": false, "prospective_role": "hold_for_date_review", "known_by_date": null, "original_csv": {"id": "DCP-LETT-690", "sender_surname": "Lindley", "sender_forename": "John", "recipient_surname": "Darwin", "recipient_forename": "C. R.", "sorting_date": "1843-09-02", "date": "[before 2 Sept 1843]", "sender_address": "unstated", "recipient_address": "", "source": "DAR 50: A21–2", "languages": "", " extent": "", " filename": "DCP-LETT-690.xml"}, "provenance": {"revision": "ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06", "csv_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/darwin-correspondence.csv", "csv_record_number": 770, "csv_physical_line_start": 773, "csv_physical_line_end": 773, "xml_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/expansions/1837-1843/letters/DCP-LETT-690.xml", "xml_sha256": "8ad535014cebded4bae3e947146553a1eec8d1cd5139afd170747652ed5da3ea", "xml_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cambridge-collection/epsilon-data/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/xml/darwin-correspondence/letters/DCP-LETT-690.xml", "letter_page_url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-690.xml", "date_xpath": "/tei:TEI/tei:teiHeader/tei:profileDesc/tei:correspDesc/tei:correspAction[@type='sent']/tei:date"}, "metadata_multiple_senders": false, "individual_voice_attribution_review_required": false}, "title": "From John Lindley [before 2 September 1843]", "header_text": ["From John Lindley [before 2 September 1843]"], "paragraphs": [{"body_paragraph": 1, "text": "I am infinitely obliged to you for your interesting communications which I wd have acknowledged sooner had I been able. The Gentians are new to me, and I think form a valuable addition to the little we know about double flowers.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"}, {"body_paragraph": 2, "text": "The Cabbage leaf is not very uncommon.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"}, {"body_paragraph": 3, "text": "Thanks too for the Viola—", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"}, {"body_paragraph": 4, "text": "You will be interested in knowing that a very curious monster found this year near Ely shows the ovule—its nucleus I mean—to be another of the forms of the growing point—quite a new, & to me at least unexpected, fact, which was much wanted to complete the theory of morphological structure. The evidence is perfect.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 4"}, {"body_paragraph": 5, "text": "Your Scotch seeds proved Rumex Acetosella & this Atriplex—What species I do not know— At present I cannot find it in books. I have sent it to Henslow and shall show it to others— It cannot be any var of A. patula I think.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 5"}, {"body_paragraph": 6, "text": "Very truly yours | John Lindley", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 6"}], "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [{"class": "salute", "text": "Dear Sir"}], "body_container_count": 1, "used_whole_body_fallback": false, "editorial_summary": "Summary Much interested in CD’s communication [about W. Kemp] and seeds sent; does not know the species; has sent seeds to Henslow. Describes a monstrous plant found near Ely.", "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1See letter to Gardeners’ Chronicle, [late August 1843].2Refers to the theory of Johann Wolfgang von Goethe that all the parts of a plant are metamorphosed leaves. CD accepted the theory as demonstrating the unity of type one would expect under an evolutionary point of view. See Foundations, pp. 38–41, 214–18. The doctrine was considered atheistical by those who maintained that each species was created perfect and immutable.3Seeds discovered by William Kemp (see letter to John Lindley, 8 [April 1843], and letter from John Lindley, [after 8 April 1843]).", "letter_container_present": true}
{"id": "DCP-LETT-701", "source": {"path": "data/raw/dcp/correspondent-review-1837-1843/seed-context/DCP-LETT-701.html", "url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-701.xml", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-16T09:41:55.852335+00:00", "sha256": "c9d37d5b25ddc5cfcb5013f64fb83c5bc988f93e1475fbd5476cbc0b56106cee", "bytes": 113257, "http_status": 200, "etag": "\"ca2bbd3e010fb85c99f1900fc3465dc3\"", "content_type": "text/html", "id": "DCP-LETT-701"}, "metadata_audit": {"id": "DCP-LETT-701", "classification": "safe_within_period", "classification_reason": "Every XML-encoded date or bound lies inside the inclusive period.", "direction": "to_darwin", "period_selection_eligible": true, "xml_earliest": "1843-10-09", "xml_latest": "1843-10-09", "date_structure": "single_xml_day", "source_date_flags": [], "single_xml_day_without_textual_qualifier": true, "exact_order_needs_review": false, "sorting_date_differs_from_xml_earliest": false, "sent_date_constraints": [{"text": "9 Oct 1843", "attributes": {"when": "1843-10-09"}, "lower": "1843-10-09", "upper": "1843-10-09", "xml_fragment": "<ns0:date xmlns:ns0=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" when=\"1843-10-09\">9 Oct 1843</ns0:date>"}], "received_date_constraints": [], "sender_evidence": [{"text": "Henslow, J. S.", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_2235.xml"}}], "recipient_evidence": [{"text": "Darwin, C. R.", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_1.xml"}}], "xml_sender_address": ["Hitcham"], "xml_notes": [{"text": "3pp", "attributes": {"type": "physdesc", "n": "ALS"}}], "has_transcription_in_preserved_xml": false, "reply_link_status": "not_audited", "training_target_eligible": false, "prospective_role": "incoming_context_pending_receipt_and_reply_evidence", "known_by_date": null, "original_csv": {"id": "DCP-LETT-701", "sender_surname": "Henslow", "sender_forename": "J. S.", "recipient_surname": "Darwin", "recipient_forename": "C. R.", "sorting_date": "1843-10-09", "date": "9 Oct 1843", "sender_address": "Hitcham", "recipient_address": "", "source": "DAR 50: A24–5", "languages": "", " extent": "", " filename": "DCP-LETT-701.xml"}, "provenance": {"revision": "ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06", "csv_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/darwin-correspondence.csv", "csv_record_number": 783, "csv_physical_line_start": 786, "csv_physical_line_end": 786, "xml_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/expansions/1837-1843/letters/DCP-LETT-701.xml", "xml_sha256": "dd4c4f63a24a0f44822758d03fecf82256d9a0600ce0a9017f93176f80b6f695", "xml_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cambridge-collection/epsilon-data/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/xml/darwin-correspondence/letters/DCP-LETT-701.xml", "letter_page_url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-701.xml", "date_xpath": "/tei:TEI/tei:teiHeader/tei:profileDesc/tei:correspDesc/tei:correspAction[@type='sent']/tei:date"}, "metadata_multiple_senders": false, "individual_voice_attribution_review_required": false}, "title": "From J. S. Henslow 9 October 1843", "header_text": ["From J. S. Henslow 9 October 1843H. H. S [Hitcham Hadleigh Suffolk]9 Oct 1843"], "paragraphs": [{"body_paragraph": 1, "text": "Specimens from Mr Kemp incline me to think that the supposed A. hastata will turn out after all to be only a strange var. of Atriplex patula a very common plant in waste lands— His other two are equally common viz. Polygonum convolvulus & aviculare— I trust there is no mistake about the seeds of these plants being in the soil he used— They are all 3 great gardening & agricultural pests— I have been so deep in the Tumulus that I have not had time to think about your quere which I will do as soon as I can— I managed to restore the Glass Urn & made a model of the brick vault— The whole was exhibited as a 1s /– show (!) at the Bury Bazaar on Saturday & realized more than 25£—which is turning a sight to some profit— They are to occupy a permanent position in the house of the Gent— on whose property they were found—", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"}, {"body_paragraph": 2, "text": "Joy of a new daughter & congratulations to Mrs D.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"}, {"body_paragraph": 3, "text": "D for ever!", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"}, {"body_paragraph": 4, "text": "D. d. Δ. δ. I don’t know Hebrew or would go on— I forgot D. d. —", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 4"}, {"body_paragraph": 5, "text": "Ever Yrs truly | J S Henslow", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 5"}], "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [{"class": "salute", "text": "My dear Darwin,"}], "body_container_count": 1, "used_whole_body_fallback": false, "editorial_summary": "Summary Thinks W. Kemp’s specimens are all common varieties of living species of Atriplex.", "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1Henslow had discovered a Roman tomb near Bury St Edmunds, Suffolk. He described the find in Henslow 1843b.2An allusion to CD’s children who are referred to as little ‘d’s (see Correspondence vol. 3, letter to Leonard Jenyns, [14 or 21 August 1846]). Before and during the Beagle voyage, CD used a seal engraved with an italic, capital ‘D’.", "letter_container_present": true}
{"id": "DCP-LETT-707", "source": {"path": "data/raw/dcp/correspondent-review-1837-1843/seed-context/DCP-LETT-707.html", "url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-707.xml", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-16T09:41:56.636504+00:00", "sha256": "aef09b1dbd58395e7e6eb2413e632e4f2827b1758ab52b1da2729d3b06e08fca", "bytes": 113690, "http_status": 200, "etag": "\"3309c82f4f4142105f8154e410d21e54\"", "content_type": "text/html", "id": "DCP-LETT-707"}, "metadata_audit": {"id": "DCP-LETT-707", "classification": "safe_within_period", "classification_reason": "Every XML-encoded date or bound lies inside the inclusive period.", "direction": "to_darwin", "period_selection_eligible": true, "xml_earliest": "1843-10-17", "xml_latest": "1843-10-17", "date_structure": "single_xml_day", "source_date_flags": [], "single_xml_day_without_textual_qualifier": true, "exact_order_needs_review": false, "sorting_date_differs_from_xml_earliest": false, "sent_date_constraints": [{"text": "17 Oct 1843", "attributes": {"when": "1843-10-17"}, "lower": "1843-10-17", "upper": "1843-10-17", "xml_fragment": "<ns0:date xmlns:ns0=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" when=\"1843-10-17\">17 Oct 1843</ns0:date>"}], "received_date_constraints": [], "sender_evidence": [{"text": "Henslow, J. S.", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_2235.xml"}}], "recipient_evidence": [{"text": "Darwin, C. R.", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_1.xml"}}], "xml_sender_address": ["Hitcham"], "xml_notes": [{"text": "4pp †", "attributes": {"type": "physdesc", "n": "ALS"}}], "has_transcription_in_preserved_xml": false, "reply_link_status": "not_audited", "training_target_eligible": false, "prospective_role": "incoming_context_pending_receipt_and_reply_evidence", "known_by_date": null, "original_csv": {"id": "DCP-LETT-707", "sender_surname": "Henslow", "sender_forename": "J. S.", "recipient_surname": "Darwin", "recipient_forename": "C. R.", "sorting_date": "1843-10-17", "date": "17 Oct 1843", "sender_address": "Hitcham", "recipient_address": "", "source": "DAR 50: A26–7", "languages": "", " extent": "", " filename": "DCP-LETT-707.xml"}, "provenance": {"revision": "ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06", "csv_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/darwin-correspondence.csv", "csv_record_number": 792, "csv_physical_line_start": 795, "csv_physical_line_end": 795, "xml_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/expansions/1837-1843/letters/DCP-LETT-707.xml", "xml_sha256": "a255a9739a95fd07c6bdf4c44ea7a61ba521defc00225f7dc4bf90bd612b7f8a", "xml_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cambridge-collection/epsilon-data/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/xml/darwin-correspondence/letters/DCP-LETT-707.xml", "letter_page_url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-707.xml", "date_xpath": "/tei:TEI/tei:teiHeader/tei:profileDesc/tei:correspDesc/tei:correspAction[@type='sent']/tei:date"}, "metadata_multiple_senders": false, "individual_voice_attribution_review_required": false}, "title": "From J. S. Henslow 17 October 1843", "header_text": ["From J. S. Henslow 17 October 1843H. H. S. [Hitcham Hadleigh Suffolk]17 Oct 1843"], "paragraphs": [{"body_paragraph": 1, "text": "The odd Atriplex came from Lindley alone — Mr K’s was clearly only A. patula, & this it is that staggers me— Lindley ought to hunt out the A. hastata in the Linnean or other herbaria in London & see what he can make of it—", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"}, {"body_paragraph": 2, "text": "The raising some of these things indoors & in pots has evidently induced an unusual habit in them— but this is a different thing from the very marked characters about the supposed A. hastata— tho’ with my usual “unwillingly discriminatory-species” eyes I can conceive A. patula & A. hastata to be the same thing—", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"}, {"body_paragraph": 3, "text": "Many more than 300, & probably double that No. came to see the Roman Tomb— The 2d day’s admission was 6d & so for several on the 1st day— I only modelled the brickwork, & then laid the articles precisely in sitû. I have drawn up a little account with a lithograph figure which I will send to London some day for you— I hope to be in town in Novr. & perhaps give a little account of my Whales ears & Nodules— I have had the 2 best specimens modelled—one of each species—", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"}, {"body_paragraph": 4, "text": "Ever Yrs truly | J S Henslow", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 4"}], "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [{"class": "salute", "text": "My dear Darwin,"}], "body_container_count": 1, "used_whole_body_fallback": false, "editorial_summary": "Summary Regards [W. Kemp’s] plant as clearly only Atriplex patula, though with \"an unusual habit\". Adds report on success of his Roman tomb exhibit.", "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1See letter from John Lindley, [before 2 September 1843], and letter from J. S. Henslow, 9 October 1843.2See letter from C. C. Babington, 26 October 1843.3Henslow 1843b.4Henslow reported to the Geological Society on 13 December on concretions, including fossil petro-tympanic bones of Cetacea, he had found in the Red Crag at Felixstowe, Suffolk (Henslow 1843c, with an appendix describing four species by Richard Owen).", "letter_container_present": true}
{"id": "DCP-LETT-708", "source": {"path": "data/raw/dcp/correspondent-review-1837-1843/seed-context/DCP-LETT-708.html", "url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-708.xml", "retrieved_at": "2026-09-16T09:41:56.615038+00:00", "sha256": "0a9e8945c214e161c3aefbd27c661a9f96268eac329cdaa05fa565cff2909d71", "bytes": 112581, "http_status": 200, "etag": "\"ef787b223778f17a128a1d9d3fa63388\"", "content_type": "text/html", "id": "DCP-LETT-708"}, "metadata_audit": {"id": "DCP-LETT-708", "classification": "safe_within_period", "classification_reason": "Every XML-encoded date or bound lies inside the inclusive period.", "direction": "to_darwin", "period_selection_eligible": true, "xml_earliest": "1843-10-26", "xml_latest": "1843-10-26", "date_structure": "single_xml_day", "source_date_flags": [], "single_xml_day_without_textual_qualifier": true, "exact_order_needs_review": false, "sorting_date_differs_from_xml_earliest": false, "sent_date_constraints": [{"text": "26 Oct 1843", "attributes": {"when": "1843-10-26"}, "lower": "1843-10-26", "upper": "1843-10-26", "xml_fragment": "<ns0:date xmlns:ns0=\"http://www.tei-c.org/ns/1.0\" when=\"1843-10-26\">26 Oct 1843</ns0:date>"}], "received_date_constraints": [], "sender_evidence": [{"text": "Babington, C. C.", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_214.xml"}}], "recipient_evidence": [{"text": "Darwin, C. R.", "attributes": {"key": "../nameregs/nameregs_1.xml"}}], "xml_sender_address": ["St John’s College, Cambridge"], "xml_notes": [{"text": "2pp", "attributes": {"type": "physdesc", "n": "ALS"}}], "has_transcription_in_preserved_xml": false, "reply_link_status": "not_audited", "training_target_eligible": false, "prospective_role": "incoming_context_pending_receipt_and_reply_evidence", "known_by_date": null, "original_csv": {"id": "DCP-LETT-708", "sender_surname": "Babington", "sender_forename": "C. C.", "recipient_surname": "Darwin", "recipient_forename": "C. R.", "sorting_date": "1843-10-26", "date": "26 Oct 1843", "sender_address": "St John’s College, Cambridge", "recipient_address": "", "source": "DAR 50: A28", "languages": "", " extent": "", " filename": "DCP-LETT-708.xml"}, "provenance": {"revision": "ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06", "csv_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/darwin-correspondence.csv", "csv_record_number": 793, "csv_physical_line_start": 796, "csv_physical_line_end": 796, "xml_path": "data/raw/epsilon/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/expansions/1837-1843/letters/DCP-LETT-708.xml", "xml_sha256": "0f6b507f205fb38c5373847968a3d6e3acda7113fd7d6dfcdb93169924f12e42", "xml_url": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/cambridge-collection/epsilon-data/ab0d973bae05b54d68d82d068211015996cfec06/xml/darwin-correspondence/letters/DCP-LETT-708.xml", "letter_page_url": "https://www.darwinproject.ac.uk/letter/?docId=letters/DCP-LETT-708.xml", "date_xpath": "/tei:TEI/tei:teiHeader/tei:profileDesc/tei:correspDesc/tei:correspAction[@type='sent']/tei:date"}, "metadata_multiple_senders": false, "individual_voice_attribution_review_required": false}, "title": "From C. C. Babington 26 October 1843", "header_text": ["From C. C. Babington 26 October 1843St John’s Coll: CambridgeOct. 26. 1843."], "paragraphs": [{"body_paragraph": 1, "text": "I am much pleased to have had an opportunity of examining the Atriplex raised from seeds found at so great a debth by Mr. Kemp.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 1"}, {"body_paragraph": 2, "text": "The specimen has all the appearance of having been grown upon a very richly manured or muddy soil, but is, as I believe I may say with the utmost confidence, a variety of the A. angustifolia. I have seen plants growing on the mud of salt marshes or close to a dung-hill that exactly resembled it in all points. The usual state of the plant is so different that I cannot wonder at botanists who have not made this unattractive genus their study refering the specimens to a wrong species.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 2"}, {"body_paragraph": 3, "text": "A. hastata is quite a different plant. I should much like to see Mr. Kemp’s specimens refered by Henslow to A. patula.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 3"}, {"body_paragraph": 4, "text": "I inclose the specimen and have only to add my earnest hope that your health is now restored to its former state of goodness.", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 4"}, {"body_paragraph": 5, "text": "Believe me to be | Most truly yours | Charles C. Babington—", "html_class": "", "locator": "div#letter div.body-content; retained body block 5"}], "excluded_body_annotations_and_salutations": [{"class": "salute", "text": "Dear Darwin,"}], "body_container_count": 1, "used_whole_body_fallback": false, "editorial_summary": "Summary Identifies Atriplex raised from seeds found by W. Kemp as A. angustifolia.", "editorial_footnotes": "Footnotes1See letter to J. S. Henslow, [14 October 1843].2See letters from J. S. Henslow, 9 October 1843 and 17 October 1843.", "letter_container_present": true}
